WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.940
<i>Teshima-san, I want to 
ride all-out to catch up.</i>

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.070
You can do it!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.490
Teshima-san!

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:17.740
Onoda!

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.160
So this is Onoda, huh? Wow.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.170
You're fast, but...

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.960
I won't let you win this race!

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.450
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.810
Ashikiba's attacking!

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.040
<i>RIDE.04 The Fastest Man on Minegayama</i>

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.160
He counterattacked the 
moment Onoda-kun caught up!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.070
Th-There's only one kilometer left!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.750
<i>A race...</i>

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.060
<i>I'm finally racing again.</i>

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.240
<i>If possible, beat him.</i>

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.500
<i>I'll win, Shinkai-san, Fukutomi-san.</i>

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:31.790
I'm glad you came.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.920
I'm glad you came, Onoda.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.060
Uh, wh-while I was watching you ride,
my body got so hot.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.840
My legs wouldn't stop pumping.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.310
I'm happy to hear that.
I'll note that in my journal.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.460
How are you feeling? Better?

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.100
How's your body? And your new bike?

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.770
Can you go after him?

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.190
Yes, sir.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.450
He seems strong. He's big and fast.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.440
But I think I can do it.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.450
He's fast?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.620
Is he faster than Makishima-san?

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.630
No, absolutely not.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:28.020
After all, Makishima-san is the fastest 
and coolest climber in the world!

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:32.060
Then go prove it by beating him!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.490
Yes, sir!

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.790
Makishima-san is...

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.870
Makishima? Who is that?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.380
Makishima-san is way, way...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.380
Faster!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.540
Yeah!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.020
<i>Goal!</i>

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.940
<i>Just as expected, the first man 
to finish is Sohoku High's Onoda!</i>

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.810
He's incredible!

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.280
<i>I said "yeah" like Makishima-san 
without thinking.</i>

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.010
<i>Second place is Hakone Academy's Ashikiba!</i>

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.610
I see. I understand now, Shinkai-san.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.260
This is Sohoku.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.500
They certainly are strong.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.450
Onoda, good job. You did great.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.920
I'm not good enough.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.480
I gave too much.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.350
Crap. That was lame.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.010
I wasn't good enough, either.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:58.180
<i>Once again, unfortunately,
Onoda failed to break the course record.</i>

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:03.860
<b>Minegayama Hill Climb Race</b>

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.820
<i>He was 34 seconds short 
of breaking the record</i>

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.860
<i>set last year by Sohoku 
High's Makishima Yuusuke.</i>

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.990
He really is amazing...

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.390
Yes, sir.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:20.500
<b>Minegayama
Hill Climb Race</b>

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:20.500
<b>Minegayama
Hill Climb Race</b>

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.380
<i>The race is over.</i>

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.920
Wait up!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:26.670
<i>Jun-chan, the next time we meet,
we'll be opponents again.</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.010
<i>And at...</i>

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.680
<i>next year's Inter-High, too.</i>

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.330
Look.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.650
He's amazing.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.020
<i>I lost.</i>

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.170
<i>They finally let me race again, and I lost.</i>

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.830
<i>Shinkai-san...</i>

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.980
<i>They expect me to be the next ace.</i>

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.630
<i>Fukutomi-san...</i>

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.550
<i>How can I apologize to them?</i>

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.230
My stop's coming up. Go ahead.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.490
Oh my, but you're a tall one.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.520
Are you sure?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.730
Yes, go ahead. It's fine.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.280
My stop...

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.930
<i>...was three stops ago.</i>

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.250
<b>Hakone Academy Bicycle Club</b>

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.250
You gave us a shock.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:43.710
I was waiting at the station with the coach,
but you never got off the train.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:47.170
Please keep your phone on.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.720
It was out of battery, so I left it.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.890
You left it? At home?

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.780
You should keep your cell phone on you.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.190
Keep my phone on me?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.640
That's a good one.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.890
It's not that funny.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:08.820
Did you show them your 
Metronome Dancing today?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.110
Were the Chiba guys scared?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.580
How did it go, Ashikiba?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.000
Did you win the race?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.430
Fukutomi-san...

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:26.980
Yes, sir.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.740
I was in all right shape.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.080
There was classical music 
playing inside my head.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:39.030
I tend to do well when that happens, 
so I was convinced I could win.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:44.570
Sohoku's first-year, Onoda, 
caught up to me in the last kilometer,

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:48.230
so I counterattacked and 
rode as hard as I could.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:53.660
The race played into my specialty, but...

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.160
In the end, he passed me.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.770
<i>I didn't win.</i>

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.620
<i>I'm sorry, Fukutomi-san.</i>

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:11.640
<i>He's the one who saved me...</i>

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.340
Ashikiba!

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.390
Could you take these?

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.020
Sure. Just leave them right there.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.640
He's "the best," right?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.400
You're slow, Ashikiba!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.540
Stop wobbling!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.980
Yes, sir.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:31.120
You're too big.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.610
You wobble so much because your 
center of gravity is high.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.390
Honestly, you may not be 
cut out for bike racing.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:40.770
Yes, sir.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.000
<i>They're right.</i>

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:51.310
<i>I could ride a bike in middle school, 
but I was ten centimeters shorter then.</i>

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.420
<i>It was so much fun.</i>

00:08:55.090 --> 00:09:00.950
<i>But now, even I feel like my 
body's heavy. I wobble too much.</i>

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>Why do I keep growing?</i>

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:07.890
<i>I can't catch up to anyone during practice.</i>

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>Miscellaneous Club Duties</b>

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:13.190
<i>Why can't I be shorter?</i>

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:23.790
What are you doing?

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.930
Shinkai-san and Fukutomi-san...

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.790
The lights were on.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.650
Do you have laundry? I'll take care of it.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:36.430
Since I'm so big, I'm the 
best at doing laundry.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:42.890
I'm actually thinking about quitting the team
and becoming a team manager instead.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.100
Ashikiba...

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.350
The only path you should take 
is the one that leads forward.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.020
What do you want to be?

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:58.490
The best ri...

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.180
Rider.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:12.610
Then raise your head and look 
upon the sights only you can see.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.340
Only you can see what you're 
looking at right now.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:22.050
You already have something others don't.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.650
But it's...

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:27.030
A disadvantage? Who decided that?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.140
You did.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.090
The only way to get stronger is to practice.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:40.280
That means training to get the 
most out of what you possess.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:44.660
If you hone it enough,
you will be able to see it...

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.120
Your own style of riding!

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.960
<i>Make the most out of what I possess!</i>

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.690
Why is he riding like that?

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.670
He's swaying his body on purpose!

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:00.920
Let's make the stem ten millimeters longer 
and raise your saddle five millimeters.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:01.720
Yes, sir.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.680
What do you like?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.810
The piano.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:07.860
Good.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.350
Use that to ride.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.110
Don't be offended.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.090
Oh, I'm not.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.200
We went to the club room that day

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.950
because we heard you were going 
to become the laundry boy.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.030
Juichi was trying to cheer you up.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.030
The laundry boy won First-Year Race B!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:39.130
<i>All right. I did it, 
Shinkai-san, Fukutomi-san!</i>

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.630
What? Me?

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.550
You want me to wear a Hakone Academy 
jersey and appear in an official race?

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.460
I'll do it! I promise I'll win!

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:56.360
<i>I was so happy then,
I thought I could do anything.</i>

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.020
<i>But reality was different.</i>

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.210
He's riding the wrong way! Watch out!

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.210
I'm placing you on house arrest indefinitely.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.840
I'm not letting you race.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:21.240
I'm sorry.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.030
I placed second.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.850
I failed to meet your expectations again.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.640
You're all talk, Ashikiba.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:35.270
I thought I'd get to hear 
you tell me you won today.

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:37.750
I'm sorry.

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.160
<i>House arrest...</i>

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.930
<i>I won't be able to race again.</i>

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.270
<i>How can I repay them?</i>

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.260
I thought you were going to repay me.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.370
You'd better win the next one.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:56.590
<i>The next one?</i>

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:01.400
Ashikiba, we never lose to 
someone who's beaten us once.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:05.830
That's the duty of Hakone Academy's ace.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.260
Yes, sir.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:14.020
He's crying and smiling at the same time...

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.470
Old man, let's settle this today.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.030
Let's see who's really 
the number one sprinter.

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:32.310
Fine. Bring it on, redhead.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.540
You, too, Aoyagi.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.800
Aren't they on the same team?

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.040
Does that mean they don't 
think we stand a chance?

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.530
There's three guys leading the race!

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:43.810
Who will win the race?

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.030
Me!

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:45.720
Me!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.720
Me, of course!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.150
<i>The road racing season runs 
from March to November.</i>

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.850
<i>This is the season's last race.</i>

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:59.150
<i>The Bay Coast Hill Climb 
is entering its final lap!</i>

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.030
N-Naruko-kun and Tadokoro-san
 are so fast. So is Aoyagi-san.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.280
They're going way faster than 
they were on the previous lap.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.620
That's because it's the final lap.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.450
Tadokoro...

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:19.480
This Criterium involves over ten laps 
of a two to three kilometer course

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.000
on closed city streets.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.380
Their positioning, corner speed, and 
sprinting power are important in this race.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:32.100
And you insisted during the meeting on 
looking toward next year's Inter-High.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:37.000
When a team enters a race 
with multiple participants,

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.400
normally they pick an ace 
and act to make him win.

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:44.940
But our sprinters are incorrigible.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:51.320
All three of those idiots are trying to win.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:55.850
I'll pull, too.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:58.780
I won't feel good about 
winning if you complain later

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:01.450
that you lost because you had to 
lead the group the whole time.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:02.920
You think you're going to win?

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.330
<i>He's moving ahead!</i>

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.670
I'll pull, too.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.170
Aoyagi!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.170
Aoyagi-san!

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.080
So the quiet one wants a fair fight, too?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.600
In other words, it'll come down 
to the sprint to the finish.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:19.100
<i>The quiet one's gotten way stronger 
over the past few months.</i>

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:22.200
<i>If I underestimate him, he'll beat me.</i>

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:26.090
The three Sohoku guys are leading the race!

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.190
Nobody can catch them!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.150
The Inter-High champions are 
way stronger than the rest!

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.850
<i>He's putting his effort 
toward the wrong thing.</i>

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.660
<i>So am I. Of course we are!</i>

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:42.170
<i>This is Tadokoro-san's last race with us!</i>

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.730
They're so fast!

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:45.920
Damn it!

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:53.390
<i>They're leaving me behind, even though 
we're all wearing Sohoku jerseys.</i>

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:55.970
<i>That's it.</i>

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:01.430
<i>They're encouraging me to make Sohoku proud 
since I'm wearing one of our jerseys.</i>

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:04.190
<i>I'll do my best.</i>

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.950
<i>It's the final corner.</i>

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.360
<i>The corner comes down to how 
we enter and pull out of it.</i>

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.950
<i>I'll enter at the narrowest possible angle.</i>

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:18.390
<i>Once my posture starts reverting, 
I'll use my dancing to jump ahead!</i>

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:19.990
<i>It's the home stretch!</i>

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:22.460
<i>It's just 500 meters to the finish line!</i>

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:27.670
<i>Tadokoro-san looked after me and Junta.</i>

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.670
Go for the finish line!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:30.840
Yes, sir!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.170
I'm sorry!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.550
I'm sorry...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.760
Tadokoro-san!

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:40.020
<i>He taught us to have 
unbreakable spirits and wills.</i>

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.710
<i>He taught us how to fight.</i>

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:47.190
<i>That's why I want to show 
him that I've grown!</i>

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:56.200
<i>I can't imagine the team without the old man.</i>

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:58.820
You're a little bean.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:02.120
<i>He never yields.</i>

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.070
<i>He always shows off.</i>

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.520
<i>And he's strong.</i>

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.540
<i>That's why...</i>

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.720
<i>I'll surpass the old man!</i>

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:17.090
And today's my last chance to do that!

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.470
That's why...

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.350
That's why I have to...

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:24.350
Win!

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.810
<i>Eighty meters left!</i>

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:30.570
<i>These kids have grown.</i>

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:33.460
<i>Aoyagi, Naruko...</i>

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:36.820
<i>Carry on the spirit of 
Sohoku's sprinters, who keep</i>

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.850
<i>charging forward even after eating pavement.</i>

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.620
I'm sweating a lot today.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.290
<i>This is your last job, Tadokoro Jin.</i>

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:53.100
<i>I'll show them, so they don't win 
and let it get to their heads.</i>

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:59.550
<i>That in this world, there are
giant walls to overcome!</i>

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.140
<i>Aoyagi, Naruko!</i>

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.420
<i>Get stronger.</i>

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:07.810
<i>Stronger, stronger, stronger!</i>

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:17.820
<i>You have to pull Sohoku now.</i>

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:25.610
<i>The winner is Sohoku third-year Tadokoro Jin!</i>

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.920
<i>That was close.</i>

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.380
<i>That was the toughest sprint so far.</i>

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.840
You don't have to look so unhappy.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.820
You were supposed to quietly 
pass the baton to us!

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.810
I did it for you guys.

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:47.990
Right, Aoyagi?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.130
Say something!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.420
Kinjou!

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.490
Good work.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:01.940
You rode well.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:06.830
Thanks, Aoyagi, Naruko.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.710
You made that a memorable race.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.990
Thank you!

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:18.760
You're unusually submissive today.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.300
Into...

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.260
A special goodbye punch!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.270
You bastards!

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.990
Aoyagi-san, run for it!

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:29.100
Sprinters...

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.570
Yeah!

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:29.100
Wait!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:35.270
Thank you for three years of membership.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:39.640
We won't get to practice with you anymore.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:45.160
We have to get serious about 
studying for exams soon.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.150
Yeah.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.660
U-Uh...

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:52.140
Um, Kinjou-san, Tadokoro-san...

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:56.130
Th-Thanks for your help. This is for you.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.720
Sure, thanks.

00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.800
Thank you.

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:03.610
I'll send this to Makishima-san.

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:06.970
He helped me a lot, too.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.410
Yeah. I'm sure he'll appreciate it.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:14.050
Although it'll be hard to tell from 
his expression if he does.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:20.820
Kinjou-san, Tadokoro-san.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.490
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:27.710
We'll keep riding just as hard as you did.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.450
Thank you.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.960
Thank you.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.930
<i>They're succeeding us, huh?</i>

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:42.920
We'll now put on a performance to
 send off the graduating upperclassmen.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:45.930
I call it "Sohoku's Giant Sprinter!"

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:50.090
I'm the Rampaging Human Warhead!

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:51.580
Hear me roar!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.200
I'm the Human Bullet Train!

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:55.650
All aboard!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.940
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.370
I'm not a tiny little bean!

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:00.690
Who are you calling a bean?

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:03.570
Don't sully my retirement!

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:07.430
<i>With the upperclassmen leaving,
we have fewer members to practice with.</i>

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:10.520
<i>At this rate, we'll...</i>

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:24.170
What'd you want to talk about, hotshot?

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:27.170
You must've noticed, too.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.220
It's about that.

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:06.820
<b>Ramen Taro
Sakura Shop</b>

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:10.100
Start!

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:10.830
Watch this!

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:11.540
Consume!

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:29.410
You're both fast, but you 
were just barely short.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:31.970
You didn't break our record.

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:33.890
<i>New store record!</i>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:33.890
<b>New
Store Record!</b>

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE  A Different Bicycle Training Ground!!</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
